## 2. Tech Stack

| Layer | Choice | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Framework** | Next.js 15 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript | One codebase for UI + API; Server Components + Route Handlers + Server Actions |
| **Styling / UI** | Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui | Fast, consistent, accessible components — ideal under time pressure |
| **Auth** | Auth.js (NextAuth v5) — Credentials provider, JWT sessions | Handles session cookies; role is embedded in the JWT for RBAC |
| **ORM** | Prisma | Type-safe schema, auto-generated client, painless MySQL migrations |
| **Database** | MySQL 8 | Relational data (users, attendance, leave) with real foreign keys |
| **Validation** | Zod | Runtime validation shared between client forms and server handlers |
| **Password hashing** | bcryptjs | Industry-standard salted hashing |
| **Deployment** | Vercel (app) + managed MySQL (Railway / Aiven / PlanetScale) | Zero-config Next.js hosting + hosted DB |

> **PlanetScale note:** if you deploy on PlanetScale, set `relationMode = "prisma"` in the
> Prisma datasource (it doesn't use traditional foreign keys). For local dev and Railway/Aiven,
> standard MySQL foreign keys work as-is.

