## 4. Data Model (ERD)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    User ||--o| EmployeeProfile : "has profile"
    User ||--o| SalaryStructure : "has salary"
    User ||--o{ AttendanceRecord : "logs"
    User ||--o{ LeaveRequest : "submits"
    User ||--o{ LeaveRequest : "reviews"
    User ||--o{ Document : "owns"

    User {
        string id PK
        string employeeId UK
        string email UK
        string passwordHash
        enum role "EMPLOYEE | ADMIN"
        datetime createdAt
        datetime updatedAt
    }
    EmployeeProfile {
        string id PK
        string userId FK "unique"
        string firstName
        string lastName
        string phone
        string address
        datetime dateOfBirth
        string profilePictureUrl
        string jobTitle
        string department
        enum employmentType
        datetime dateOfJoining
    }
    SalaryStructure {
        string id PK
        string userId FK "unique"
        decimal basic
        decimal hra
        decimal allowances
        decimal deductions
        string currency
        datetime effectiveFrom
    }
    AttendanceRecord {
        string id PK
        string userId FK
        date date
        datetime checkIn
        datetime checkOut
        enum status "PRESENT | ABSENT | HALF_DAY | LEAVE"
        decimal workHours
    }
    LeaveRequest {
        string id PK
        string userId FK "requester"
        enum type "PAID | SICK | UNPAID"
        date startDate
        date endDate
        string remarks
        enum status "PENDING | APPROVED | REJECTED"
        string reviewedById FK "reviewer, nullable"
        string reviewerComment
    }
    Document {
        string id PK
        string userId FK
        string name
        string url
        datetime uploadedAt
    }
```

### Key rules & constraints

- `User.employeeId` and `User.email` are **unique**.
- `AttendanceRecord` has a **composite unique** `(userId, date)` — one attendance row per employee per day.
- `LeaveRequest` has **two relations** to `User`: the requester (`userId`) and the reviewer (`reviewedById`, nullable, set on approve/reject).
- Deleting a `User` cascades to profile, salary, attendance, leave, and documents.
- Money fields use `Decimal(12,2)` — never store currency as floats.

The full, runnable schema lives in [`prisma/schema.prisma`](./prisma/schema.prisma).

