## 5. API Surface

Auth endpoints are provided by Auth.js at `/api/auth/*`. Everything below is protected — the
handler resolves the session, then applies role checks. `own` = employee limited to their own
records; `all` = Admin/HR.

| Method | Endpoint | Access | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/register` | Public | Create account (employeeId, email, password, role) |
| `GET/POST` | `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` | Public | Sign in / sign out / session (Auth.js) |
| `GET` | `/api/me` | Authenticated | Current user + profile |
| `GET` | `/api/employees` | Admin | List employees (search + pagination) |
| `GET` | `/api/employees/:id` | Admin | Single employee detail |
| `GET` | `/api/profile/:userId` | own / Admin | View profile |
| `PATCH` | `/api/profile/:userId` | own (limited) / Admin (all) | Update profile |
| `POST` | `/api/attendance/check-in` | Employee (self) | Record check-in for today |
| `POST` | `/api/attendance/check-out` | Employee (self) | Record check-out; compute work hours |
| `GET` | `/api/attendance?userId=&from=&to=` | own / Admin (all) | Daily/weekly attendance |
| `GET` | `/api/leaves` | own / Admin (all) | List leave requests |
| `POST` | `/api/leaves` | Employee | Apply for leave |
| `PATCH` | `/api/leaves/:id` | Admin | Approve / reject + comment |
| `GET` | `/api/payroll/:userId` | own (read-only) / Admin | View salary structure |
| `PATCH` | `/api/payroll/:userId` | Admin | Update salary structure |

> **Convention:** Every handler `(1)` resolves the session via `auth()`, `(2)` validates the body
> with a Zod schema, `(3)` authorizes (own-or-admin), then `(4)` calls a service function. Mutations
> that back a form may instead be implemented as **Server Actions** with identical guards.

