## 6. Authentication & RBAC

### Sign-up / sign-in flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant B as Browser
    participant R as Route Handler / Auth.js
    participant DB as MySQL (via Prisma)

    B->>R: POST /api/auth/register (employeeId, email, password, role)
    R->>R: Validate (Zod) + bcrypt.hash(password)
    R->>DB: INSERT User (+ empty EmployeeProfile, SalaryStructure)
    DB-->>R: User created
    R-->>B: 201 Created

    B->>R: signIn(credentials) → /api/auth/callback/credentials
    R->>DB: SELECT User by email
    DB-->>R: User (passwordHash, role)
    R->>R: bcrypt.compare(password, hash)
    R-->>B: Set httpOnly JWT session cookie (role embedded)
```

### Role-based access control

- **Roles:** `EMPLOYEE` (default) and `ADMIN` (HR Officer).
- The role is written into the JWT in the Auth.js `jwt` callback and surfaced in `session` so it's
  available on both server and client without an extra DB hit.
- **Edge guard (`middleware.ts`):** unauthenticated users hitting `/dashboard/**` are redirected to
  `/login`; non-admins hitting `/dashboard/admin/**` are redirected to their own dashboard.
- **Handler guard:** every API route re-checks the session server-side (never trust the client),
  enforcing `own-or-admin` on record-level access.

```
Public            → /login, /register
EMPLOYEE + ADMIN  → /dashboard, /profile, /attendance, /leaves, /payroll
ADMIN only        → /dashboard/admin/**  (employees, attendance, leave approvals, payroll edit)
```

