## 10. 8-Hour MVP Build Plan

A realistic, dependency-ordered timeline. Commit at the end of each block so you always have a
working checkpoint.

| Block | Time | Deliverable |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **0** | 0:00–0:30 | Scaffold `create-next-app` (TS, Tailwind, App Router), init shadcn/ui, `git init`, **push initial commit** (this README + `.env.example`) |
| **1** | 0:30–1:30 | MySQL + `schema.prisma` + `migrate dev` + `prisma.ts` singleton + `seed.ts` (admin + 2 employees) |
| **2** | 1:30–2:45 | Auth.js config, `/api/auth/register`, login & register pages, `middleware.ts` RBAC, session type augmentation |
| **3** | 2:45–3:30 | Dashboard shell: role-aware sidebar/nav, employee vs admin landing pages |
| **4** | 3:30–4:30 | Profile view + limited edit (employee) / full edit (admin); Payroll **read-only** view + admin edit |
| **5** | 4:30–6:00 | Attendance: check-in/out endpoints + daily/weekly views (employee own, admin all) |
| **6** | 6:00–7:15 | Leave: apply form + list (employee); approve/reject + comment (admin) |
| **7** | 7:15–8:00 | Polish, empty/error states, re-seed, deploy to Vercel + managed MySQL, final commit + buffer |

**Time-saving tips**

- Lean on shadcn/ui `Table`, `Card`, `Dialog`, `Badge`, `Form` — don't hand-roll components.
- Use **Server Components** for all reads (no client fetching boilerplate).
- Prefer **Server Actions** for the leave/attendance/profile forms to skip writing separate fetch calls.
- Seed generously so every screen has data to render immediately.
- If you fall behind: ship Attendance + Leave first (highest-value workflows), then Profile/Payroll.

