## 11. Non-Functional Requirements

- **Security** — bcrypt password hashing; httpOnly, signed JWT session cookies; server-side RBAC on
  every mutation; Zod validation on all inputs; Prisma parameterizes queries (SQL-injection safe).
- **Authorization integrity** — never trust client-supplied role or `userId`; always derive identity
  from the session and re-check ownership.
- **Performance** — indexed lookups (`role`, `date`, `status`, `userId`); paginate list endpoints.
- **Data integrity** — unique constraints (`email`, `employeeId`, `userId+date`); `Decimal` for money.
- **Maintainability** — business rules isolated in `lib/services`; single source of truth for the
  schema; typed end-to-end (Prisma types → Zod → components).

